@* A page this front end does not have yet: one plain line and the same place in the classic front end (never a fake
   page). The classic pages share this browser's session cookie, so the link opens there at once; classic=1 takes it
   past the swap's redirect (the classic pages stay one release). *@
<section class="area-page not-yet">
    <h1>@Title</h1>
    <p>
        @Title is not in the Blazor front end yet.
        <a href="@PastTheSwap">Open in the classic front end</a>
    </p>
</section>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string Title { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>The classic front end's address for the same place.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string Classic { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    private string PastTheSwap => Classic + (Classic.Contains('?', StringComparison.Ordinal) ? "&classic=1" : "?classic=1");
}
